# Build artifacts
build/bin/
build/log/
build/release/
build/darwin/
build/windows/
build/linux/
internal/archive/build/
DixieData
DixieData.exe
*.exe
*.test

# Frontend build outputs
frontend/dist/
frontend/app.css
frontend/wailsjs/
frontend/node_modules/
node_modules/

# Templ generated files
internal/templates/*_templ.go
internal/releasehistory/baked.go
internal/templates/*_templ.txt
*_templ.go
*_templ.txt

# Database files (user data)
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*-wal
*-shm
*-journal

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
.cursor/
.aider*

# User data directory
.dixiedata/
.dixiedata-logs/
.dixiedata-state/
dixiedata-backup-*.ddbak

# Go test cache
*.out
coverage.out
*.prof

# Project secrets + telemetry
google-oauth-defaults.json
feedback.jsonl

# Releases + test artifacts
release/
tests/goldmaster/artifacts/
tests/stress/artifacts/
tests/goldmaster/playwright/node_modules/
tests/goldmaster/playwright/test-results/
tests/goldmaster/playwright/playwright-report/

# Copilot transient
.copilot-temp/

# rpiv-workflow runtime state
.rpiv/runs/
.rpiv/workflows/runs/
# Issue drafts and design artifacts are tracked. The .rpiv/artifacts/
# tree is a mixed convention — runtime state (discover/, research/,
# plans/, designs/, handoffs/, validation/) is gitignored; durable
# issue bodies and design docs that need to ship with the code are
# tracked under .rpiv/artifacts/issues/ and
# .rpiv/artifacts/designs-published/.
.rpiv/artifacts/discover/
.rpiv/artifacts/research/
.rpiv/artifacts/plans/
.rpiv/artifacts/designs/
.rpiv/artifacts/handoffs/
.rpiv/artifacts/validation/
!.rpiv/artifacts/issues/
!.rpiv/artifacts/issues/**

# Session-local survey source material (digested into docs/agents/pdf-field-survey.json)
TDM65-*.pdf

# my-skills-framework — symlinks are project-local, regenerated by bootstrap
.pi/skills/

# PDF render artifacts. docs/renderings/<surface>/{pre-iteration,round-*}
# are regenerated by `make render-round` and are not source — the
# source is templates/*.typ. review.md, README.md, and
# TERMINOLOGY.md remain tracked.
docs/renderings/**/pre-iteration.pdf
docs/renderings/**/round-*.pdf
# Native-SVG and PNG preview artifacts written by `make render-svg`
# (or render-svg.sh). Multi-page surfaces emit one file per page
# (round-{N,p}.svg), so these can balloon quickly during iteration.
docs/renderings/**/round-*.svg
docs/renderings/**/round-*.png

# UI/UX audit harness (issue #74). The harness reports/screenshots are
# regenerated by `node audit/run.mjs` and friends; only the harness
# sources and JSON reports are tracked.
audit/screenshots/
audit/screenshots-r2/
audit/screenshots-r3/
audit/screenshots-interactive/
audit/audit-interactive-report.json
# ui-diff screenshots (issue #74 PR4) are regenerated by `make ui-diff`;
# the JSON summary lands in audit/reports/ui-diff/summary.json and is
# tracked so visual diffs are auditable in git history.
audit/reports/ui-diff/*.png
audit/reports/phase3-after-*.png

# dixiedata-web scratch data dir. Web-mode runs write a sqlite db + images
# here so they don't touch .dixiedata/. Regenerated by `make web-run` +
# `make web-seed`.
.scratch/
# Audit-harness variant of the scratch dir. `audit/smoke_*.mjs` probes
# spawn `dixiedata-web` against this dir + seed it via `seed-data`, then
# tear it down in `finally`. Survives across runs only when a probe
# crashes mid-flight without cleanup.
.dixiedata-web-scratch/

# Bug Hunter skill working directory (per skill spec: 'Add .bug-hunter/ to your project's .gitignore')
.bug-hunter/
audit/manual-walk-report.json

# Consensus Hunter skill working directory
.consensus-hunter/

# pi scratch (transient diagnostic / listing scripts run by pi agents)
.pi/scratch/

# rpiv scratch (transient content for skill workflows)
.rpiv/scratch/

# Build-time debug + server stdout logs (regenerated each run)
build/*.log

# Audit scratch outputs (smoke .tmp files; phase reports are local-only)
audit/smoke_*.mjs.tmp

# Python REPL scratch (per docs/agents/repl.md). The `repl` skill is a
# scratch tool for deterministic investigation — Python scripts are
# NEVER part of the Go build and NEVER imported by Go code. Scratch
# lives in /tmp, tools/scratch/, or .scratch/. If a script proves
# useful enough to keep, port to Go.
tools/scratch/
*.py
!tools/scratch/.gitkeep

# Per-iteration PDF artifacts (Typst rendering iteration). The
# source `.typ` templates are tracked; these PDFs are regenerated
# by `make render-round` for each round. Old rounds move to
# docs/historical/renderings/ when the retention rule fires.
docs/renderings/*/pre-iteration.pdf
docs/renderings/*/round-*.pdf

# Release state sidecar JSONs written by
# `scripts/bump-version.ps1 -BumpUpdateFlow`. Each U bump archives
# the previous sequence's last N here so a future U-bump can be
# reviewed. These are operational artifacts; the release line
# itself lives in internal/versioninfo/versioninfo.go (tracked).
.release-state/
.dixiedata-cookies/
